  "notes": [
    "How it works: Cracker's Wither Storm from Minecraft is drawn into GTA V Legacy story mode, where it grows over Los Santos and pulls in and devours real GTA people and cars. You play Steve in creative mode, driven by GTA's movement and camera.",
    "Press Play: Minecraft 1.20.1 (Forge, with the Wither Storm mod) starts first and loads its creative \"passthrough\" world by itself; leave its window open. GTA V then starts with BattlEye off: pick Story Mode yourself. GTA shows \"Minecraft passthrough connected\" and the storm keys when linked.",
    "Keys: F9 summons a storm ahead of you (Shift+F9 an already grown one), F10 advances its phase, F11 removes it (Shift+F11 starts its death). F7 toggles the passthrough, F8 re-levels the Minecraft ground. Mouse: Minecraft attack/use, wheel or 1-9 the hotbar, Tab gun modes.",
    "You need GTA V Legacy on Steam (GTA5.exe; not the Enhanced edition) and Minecraft: Java Edition, on Windows. Install ScriptHookV for your GTA build yourself (up to build 3889): copy ScriptHookV.dll and dinput8.dll from its bin folder into the GTA V folder.",
    "Use a Story Mode save past the prologue: the mod is on from the start, so press F7 to turn it off, play the opening mission, then press F7 again in Los Santos. Story mode only, never GTA Online: BattlEye stays off while installed. Back up your saves first.",
    "The local link has no password while Minecraft runs. Beta, experimental upstream (issue #1 reports a third-person lock and ghosting): report bugs to the author with the Report a bug link."
  ]
}
